{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DZfXL4CkN9yYHpuvH6dE6B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: SunMicrosystems */\n2\t/* Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. */\n3\t\n4\t/**\n5\t *\n6\t * This family of functions computes the binary exponent of the input value as\n7\t * a signed integer.\n8\t *\n9\t * Synopsis\n10\t * ========\n11\t *\n12\t * .. code-block:: c\n13\t *\n14\t *     #include <math.h>\n15\t *     int ilogbf(float x);\n16\t *     int ilogb(double x);\n17\t *     int ilogbl(long double x);\n18\t *\n19\t * Description\n20\t * ===========\n21\t *\n22\t * ``ilogb`` computes the binary exponent of the input value as a signed integer.\n23\t *\n24\t * ``ilogb`` and :ref:`logb` have the same functionality, but ``ilogb`` returns\n25\t * the binary exponent as a signed integer while :ref:`logb` returns a\n26\t * floating-point value.\n27\t *\n28\t * Mathematical Function\n29\t * =====================\n30\t *\n31\t * .. math::\n32\t *\n33\t *    ilogb(x) \\approx \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor\n34\t *\n35\t * Returns\n36\t * =======\n37\t *\n38\t * ``ilogb`` returns the binary exponent of the input value, in the range\n39\t * :math:`\\mathbb{I}`.\n40\t *\n41\t * Exceptions\n42\t * ==========\n43\t *\n44\t * Raise ``invalid operation`` exception when the correct result is not\n45\t * representable as an integer. This is the case when the input value is zero,\n46\t * infinite or :math:`NaN`, or the magnitude of the result is too large to be\n47\t * represented as an integer.\n48\t *\n49\t * Output map\n50\t * ==========\n51\t *\n52\t * +--------------+------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------+------------+\n53\t * | **x**        | :math:`-Inf`           | :math:`<0 \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor \\notin \\mathbb{I} \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor > 0` | :math:`<0 \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor \\in \\mathbb{I}`    | :math:`<0 \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor \\notin \\mathbb{I} \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor < 0` | :math:`-0` | :math:`+0` |\n54\t * \n55\t * | **ilogb(x)** | max :math:`\\mathbb{I}` | max :math:`\\mathbb{I}`                                                                                   | :math:`\\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor`                             | min :math:`\\mathbb{I}`                                                                                   | min :math:`\\mathbb{I}`  |\n56\t * +--------------+------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+--------------+----------+\n57\t *\n58\t * +--------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+\n59\t * | **x**        | :math:`>0 \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor \\notin \\mathbb{I} \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor < 0` | :math:`<0 \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor \\in \\mathbb{I}`    | :math:`>0 \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor \\notin \\mathbb{I} \\wedge \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor > 0` | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`NaN`  |\n60\t * \n61\t * | **ilogb(x)** | min :math:`\\mathbb{I}`                                                                                   | :math:`\\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor`                             | max :math:`\\mathbb{I}`                                                                                   | max :math:`\\mathbb{I}`      |\n62\t * +--------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+\n63\t *\n64\t * .. raw:: html\n65\t *\n66\t *    <!--\n67\t *    TODO: Check usefulness of this output map as well as the exception, as I\n68\t *    think the magnitude of the result can only exceed the integer range if\n69\t *    the size of ``int`` is smaller than [-1074,1023]. So the POSIX/C/etc.\n70\t *    issues may not apply to our use-cases.\n71\t *    -->\n72\t *\n73\t */\n74\t\n75\t#include <math.h>\n76\t#include \"../common/tools.h\"\n77\t\n78\t#ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS\n79\t\n80\tint ilogb(double x)\n81\t{\n82\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ\n83\t    x *= __volatile_one;\n84\t#endif /* defined(__LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ) */\n85\t\n86\t    int32_t hx, lx, ix;\n87\t\n88\t    EXTRACT_WORDS(hx, lx, x);\n89\t    hx &= 0x7fffffff;\n90\t\n91\t    if (hx < 0x00100000) {\n92\t        if ((hx | lx) == 0) {\n93\t            (void) __raise_invalid();\n94\t            return FP_ILOGB0;    /* ilogb(0) = special case error */\n95\t        } else {         /* subnormal x */\n96\t            if (hx == 0) {\n97\t                for (ix = -1043; lx > 0; lx <<= 1) {\n98\t                    ix -= 1;\n99\t                }\n100\t            } else {\n101\t                for (ix = -1022, hx <<= 11; hx > 0; hx <<= 1) {\n102\t                    ix -= 1;\n103\t                }\n104\t            }\n105\t        }\n106\t\n107\t        return ix;\n108\t    } else if (hx < 0x7ff00000) {\n109\t        return (hx >> 20) - 1023;\n110\t    } else if (hx > 0x7ff00000) {\n111\t        (void) __raise_invalid();\n112\t        return FP_ILOGBNAN;     /* NAN */\n113\t    } else {\n114\t        (void) __raise_invalid();\n115\t        return INT_MAX;         /* infinite */\n116\t    }\n117\t}\n118\t\n119\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS\n120\t\n121\tint ilogbl(long double x)\n122\t{\n123\t    return ilogb((double) x);\n124\t}\n125\t\n126\t#endif /* #ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS */\n127\t#endif /* #ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS */\n128\t\n[result-id: r66]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V6KjeM6dqaB1daWpinAsZW","session_id":"87608f66-2ae1-44b1-899e-815f34b5df7b","uuid":"37e15840-6696-4aa8-8ef3-e07970b97035","timestamp":"2026-04-08T14:51:17.561Z"}
